WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.380
Good Morning John,
I love audio books.

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:05.800
Like I love them a LOT.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:10.520
And not in that like, “Oh, well I don’t
have that much time to read anymore, and so

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:14.660
I mostly just listen to audiobooks because that's
better than not reading at all" kind of way.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:19.660
No, I love them on their own
as a medium. I find them wonderful!

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:25.360
I love book book reading as well! I love cascading
into this story, into this physical object

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:30.340
that has all these marks on a page
that turn into this story in my mind.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:34.220
There's nothing in the world like that.
But there's also nothing in the world

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:38.720
like being told a story.
That’s the oldest thing there is.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:42.960
That and like maybe music.
I think it's like what made us humans.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.300
And maybe like music and stories
at the same time?

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:50.180
Is every song a story?
Think about it and get back to me.

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:55.300
There’s been a fair amount of talk about whether
listening to an audiobook counts as reading,

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.100
or if it's like "cheating."

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.670
These conversations to me seem to be based
in two different things.

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:03.370
One, like scientifically, psychologically
is it the same?

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:06.420
No! Like subjectively I can say
that it's not the same.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:12.560
A narrator of an audiobook makes a bunch of decisions
for me before the information gets to my brain.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:16.400
I might be making some of those decisions
differently, so I think the story

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.980
is in some ways slightly different
when it's being read to me.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:26.200
And it seems like retention is measurably better
on average when read rather than when being read to.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:29.200
But that's on average, and it's actually
different from person to person.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:32.920
This to me doesn't seem like a judgment
of better or worse. It seems like

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:38.290
it's marginally different. Like not tremendously!
But somewhat different.

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:41.160
The second place that this conversation
comes from, though, is I think

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:45.440
from people who have a lot of pride
in their identity as a reader

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:47.400
or as a reader of a lot of books.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:51.760
Some people love reading lots of books,
and they see that as part of what makes them

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:53.560
valuable and exceptional.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:55.260
And I think those people are kind of just saying like,

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:58.720
"Part of why I'm proud of myself
is that I read a lot of books.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:01.320
And the fact that like somebody got through
a lot of books in audio form

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.260
isn’t the same
as the thing that I’m proud of."

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:08.140
A lot of people push back against this as
like exclusionary, but like...

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:11.700
All forms of exceptionality are exclusionary.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:15.840
We have a really hard time as humans
figuring out why we matter.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:19.910
And there are much worse ways to find pride
than, like, the length of your book list.

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:22.440
But I’m never going to be one of those people
who reads a lot of books in a year.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:23.750
I am very mildly dyslexic.

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:27.960
According to this staples.com reading test,
I read slower than the average eighth grader.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.260
But that doesn’t mean that I don’t love reading.
I totally do.

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:33.600
And it doesn't mean that audiobooks
are a replacement for books for me.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:37.540
I like audiobooks as a way
to enjoy a story.

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:41.660
To me, media is about like
enjoying being a human.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:44.860
And loving having a good story
told to me by a good storyteller is

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:50.560
probably something that I have in common
with every single one of my human ancestors.

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:52.600
And that's... pretty cool.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:58.480
And it's part of why I pushed pretty hard for our new year
of Life’s Library to have an audiobook option.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:03.680
So now you can be a part of this community of readers
all consuming the same stuff and connecting about it.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:08.160
And when you sign up, you can choose the audio
version with digital perks or with physical perks.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:10.880
And every time we start a new book,
you’ll get a code emailed to you.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:15.820
You click on that code, and into your libro.fm account
will arrive the new book.

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:19.420
I'm curating a month of this year's Life Library.
I chose a book that I have read

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:22.800
both in book form and audio form.
So I know it's good both ways.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:26.480
We decided to do this with Libro.fm
because they are just great!

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:29.740
You don’t have to be a paying member of Libro.fm
to get your book, but you can be!

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:33.820
And if you are, you get to choose which bookstore
you would like to order your audiobooks from

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:36.520
so you can support bookstores in your community.

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:39.180
And of course, just like with regular books,
you get to keep your audiobook

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:41.260
even if you cancel your Life’s Library subscription.

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:44.840
So join Life’s Library! There's a link in the
description, or you can just click right there.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:48.400
I had to put a video here because
YouTube doesn't let us link to anything

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:51.560
unless we also link to a video.
I don't know why!

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:52.580
I find it annoying.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:53.860
John I’ll see you on Tuesday.

